# Community features (member accounts + the shared commons).
#
# Both are safe to expose in a browser build: the anon key is public by design,
# and what it can do is bounded by the row-level security policies in
# supabase/schema.sql — not by keeping it secret.
#
# Leave this file uncopied and Zuri runs exactly as before: a static, offline
# PWA with no accounts and no network dependency. That is a supported mode,
# not a degraded one.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your Supabase project
# (Dashboard → Project Settings → API).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-KEY
